@startuml graph-walk-sequence
' Sources:
'   service/packs (packs.infra.api): PackRegistrationController
'   service/packs (packs.domain.rules): PackRulesets; (packs.application): PackRefusals
'   service/kernel: Rationale, Reason, CharterRefusal
'   Decided: ADR-0082. Built (slices 1 to 3): ValidationWalker, PackGraph, Scope, Origin; the registration flow below is the target.
'   The refusal mapping keeps ADR-0075 / PR #618 D1: one fault answers exactly as before.
!include _style.iuml
title API pack registration through one graph walk (target flow, ADR-0082)

actor Client
participant "PackRegistrationController\n(driving adapter)" as API
participant "Registration use case\n(packs.application)" as App
participant "PackRulesets\n(rule factory)" as Factory
participant "ValidationWalker" as Walker
participant "PackGraph" as Graph
participant "PackRefusals" as Refusals

Client -> API : POST /packs (pack archive)
API -> App : submit(pack)
App --> API : job
API --> Client : 202 Accepted, Location: /pack-registrations/{id}
note over App : the registration job runs the walk
App -> App : resolve the active set to pack ids\n(before the walk; no repository call from a predicate)
App -> Factory : rules and scope for a registration
Factory --> App : rules per node kind, predicates, the edges each check follows,\nScope(roots, selection)
App -> Walker : build(rules, predicates, phases)
App -> Graph : walk(scope, walker)
loop each node, in stable order (pack id, then URN; edges in declared order)
  Graph -> Walker : onNode(node)
  Walker -> Walker : predicate holds? then rule.apply(node)
  Walker -> Walker : append each Reason, with its Origin,\nto the Rationale
  Walker --> Graph : Descent
  Graph -> Walker : onRelationship(edge)
  Walker -> Walker : domain edge filter: does this check follow this EdgeKind?
  Walker --> Graph : Descent
end
Graph --> App
App -> Walker : rationale()
Walker --> App : Rationale
note right of Walker
  Built (slice 3): the walker's ledger is a Ledger of ClosureFaults,
  which settles on Rationale with slice 7.
end note
note right of Walker
  Phase gate: a violation in one phase
  (compose, relations including the edge-index
  rules, own closure) skips the later phases,
  so a client sees the root cause.
end note

alt the Rationale holds no violation
  App -> App : commit the pack; the job ends succeeded
else the Rationale holds a violation
  App -> Refusals : of(rationale)
  Refusals --> App : CharterRefusal (code of the first fault, every violation)
  App -> App : the job ends refused, carrying the refusal
end
Client -> API : GET /pack-registrations/{id}
API --> Client : PackRegistrationStatus: succeeded, or refused\nwith the problem (code, every violation)

note over Client, Refusals
  pack-doctor takes the same path: PackCheck asks PackRulesets for the rules and a determined selection,
  walks with the same ValidationWalker, and PackVerdicts maps the Rationale to the report and the exit code.
end note
@enduml
